  "body": "we have two functions for getting the version of a room from the database, `get_room_version_id` and `get_room_version`. The former gets the raw string, and then caches it to speed up future lookups. The second looks up the raw string, and then consults the list of known room versions to decode it into a `RoomVersion` object. The problem is that it doesn't cache the result, so is generally slower than it should be.\r\n\r\nIf `get_room_version` needs to exist at all, it should probably just wrap `get_room_version_id`.",
